        "original_id": "d2480c89-9e1a-5d85-bd1a-36cba3519001",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ray Ruffels, Bob Hewitt, William Bowrey, Frew McMillan\n- Topics: Tennis, Australian Open, citizenship, doubles championships\n\nFacts:\n- Frew McMillan was born on 20 May 1942 and became a South African former professional male tennis player.\n- Ray Ruffels was born on 23 March 1946 in Sydney and became an Australian former professional tennis player and coach.\n- In 1967, Bob Hewitt became a South African citizen after marrying a South African.\n- At the 1969 Australian Open men’s singles event, defending champion William Bowrey lost in the quarterfinals to Ray Ruffels.\n- Frew McMillan won five major doubles championships, including three Wimbledon titles with Bob Hewitt.",
